# Synapse — continuous memory loop (Cursor)

This project uses a Synapse vault (Karpathy LLM Wiki): plain Markdown you own,
queried before work and grown after meaningful sessions.

Vault path (resolved by the CLI; override with `BRAIN_VAULT`):
`$BRAIN_VAULT` — typically `~/Synapse/vault`.

## Every turn (Phase 0)

Before planning or editing on a non-trivial request:

1. Run `synapse query "<user topic>"` (or `synapse search "<topic>"` if no index).
2. Open `$BRAIN_VAULT/hot.md` and any top-ranked notes (`summary:` first).
3. Reuse vault knowledge instead of re-deriving it. Cite pages as `[[page-name]]`.

Skip for typos, formatting-only, or purely executional tasks with complete instructions
(Phase 0-short: `hot.md` + targeted search only).

## After meaningful work (Phase 2)

If you learned a pattern, decision, non-obvious fix, or anything a future agent should
not re-derive:

1. Prefer update over duplicate: `synapse search "<topic>"` first.
2. File new knowledge: `synapse file <category> <title>` then fill the body, **or**
   update an existing note and bump `updated`.
3. Cross-link with at least one `[[wikilink]]`; update `index.md` / `hot.md` / `log.md`
   if the CLI did not.
4. Run `synapse lint --strict` and fix every warning, then re-run until clean.

Categories (core): `concepts` · `techniques` · `projects` · `skills`.
Optional on demand: `sources` · `analysis` · `people` · `organizations` · `journal`.

## Session hygiene

- `synapse status` / `synapse doctor` when the vault looks wrong.
- `synapse metrics` to see if distillation has stalled.
- Schema and workflow: `$BRAIN_VAULT/AGENTS.md`, `$BRAIN_VAULT/_meta/workflow.md`.
